{% import "_macros.j2" as m %}
{# One exhibit, edge to edge under the normal header. This is a full-bleed slide, so it emits its
   own `.stage` instead of calling `stage(s)`: the shared stage pads every side, and that padding
   is exactly what this template exists to remove below the header. Consequences on purpose —
   no `.cfit`, so the content-fit pass leaves it alone (the image is sized by CSS to the box it is
   given, and a long title shrinks that box rather than overflowing it), and no highlights band or
   aside column, neither of which belongs on a slide whose whole body is the picture.
   The one exception is a `source` highlight: a picture without its citation is a picture someone
   cannot check, so that band (and only that kind) sits under the fill, and the fill gives up the
   height it needs.
   `s.image` is polymorphic exactly as `media` is (`m.smedia`): a picture or clip `{src,alt}`, or
   a code panel `{code, language}` — an un-rendered ASCII figure in the live `--draft` view. #}
{% set hlsrc = (s.highlights or []) | selectattr('kind', 'eq', 'source') | list %}
<div class="stage imgfull">
<div class="shead">{{ m.header(s) }}</div>
<div class="iffill">{{ m.smedia(s.image) }}</div>
{% if hlsrc %}{{ m.hlband(hlsrc, ' hl-source', '') }}{% endif %}
</div>
